WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.565
A live race now starts together: a countdown in the lobby, and every rider's clock

00:00:07.565 --> 00:00:09.324
on the same server time.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.232
At three seconds the countdown covers the lobby, ready or not: three, two, one, and

00:00:15.232 --> 00:00:15.709
Go.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.122
At Go the race opens, joins its session again on its own connection, and hears the

00:00:28.122 --> 00:00:30.034
start as the server's time.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.072
Its clock runs from that start, corrected by the measured offset, so a rider who

00:00:41.072 --> 00:00:43.286
opens late reads the same time.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:52.791
The countdown fills every screen, from a phone to a desktop.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.497
What the tests prove: three, two, one and Go, the seat kept past the start, and

00:01:06.497 --> 00:01:08.354
every clock on server time.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.869
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:17.214 --> 00:01:21.726
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:21.726 --> 00:01:23.397
every hill and interval.

00:01:23.742 --> 00:01:28.920
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.368
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:37.358
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:40.196
A custom workout lives under Profile.
